---
// B970 — bespoke in-kernel reconstruction.
//
// Signature layout, rebuilt 1:1 from the owned reference screenshot: every
// word the page owns lives in a single band on the top baseline, set across
// a twelve-column grid as 3/3/6 — identity stack, italic serif title with
// its roman credit, and one serif paragraph closed by a Read more link.
// Everything below the band is artwork, run full bleed to all four edges.
// The mechanic is live where the source is live — Read more extends the
// essay in place; the band never moves. The film still is echoed, not
// pictured: the room inverts to an ink field with a tonal mass where the
// portrait sat, and the plate is credited with a mono specimen label. All
// spacing/type composes from kernel custom properties.
import { getEntry } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import CaseStudy from '../../components/CaseStudy.astro';

const entry = await getEntry('works', 'b970');
const w = entry!.data;
---

<Base title={`${w.title} — *blue red + purple/`}>
  <CaseStudy work={w} stageLabel="Reconstruction — live, expanding essay band">
    <Fragment slot="narrative">
      <section class="prose">
        <h2>The signature</h2>
        <p>
          The whole voice of the page is one band across the top: a wordmark with two underlined
          links, an italic serif title over its roman credit, and a four-line essay — three, three
          and six columns of a twelve-column grid, all hung from the same baseline. The remaining
          ninety percent of the viewport belongs to a full-bleed monochrome still, and the text
          never descends into it. One Read more link is the only door the band offers.
        </p>
      </section>
    </Fragment>

    <div class="site">
      <div class="site__band">
        <header class="band__id">
          <span class="band__wordmark">{w.title} Archive</span>
          <span class="band__links" aria-hidden="true">
            <u>Contact</u>, <u>IG</u>
          </span>
        </header>

        <div class="band__caption">
          <em class="band__title">A Field in Three Columns</em>
          <span class="band__credit font-mono">{w.title}</span>
        </div>

        <div class="band__essay lh-copy">
          <p>
            The page keeps its entire voice in this one strip: an identity, an italic title with
            its credit, and a single paragraph, divided three, three and six across twelve
            columns. Everything beneath the strip is given to the artwork, which runs full bleed
            to every edge of the viewport.
          </p>
          <p class="band__extra">
            The band itself never moves. Extending the essay pushes nothing but these lines; the
            field below absorbs the rest, and the two registers never compete.
          </p>
          <button class="band__more" type="button" aria-expanded="false">Read more</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <span class="site__plate font-mono ttu" aria-hidden="true">Plate 01 — 16 mm still</span>
    </div>

    <Fragment slot="notes">
      <section class="prose">
        <h2>Study notes</h2>
        <p>
          The 3/3/6 split works because the columns widen with the weight of their content — a
          two-line identity, a two-line caption, a full paragraph — so the band reads left to
          right as an accelerating sentence. Pinning all three to one baseline is what buys the
          full-bleed image its silence: the eye clears the text in a single pass and drops into
          the still with nothing left to negotiate. The serif display against semi-mono captions
          keeps the registers legible even at one shared type size.
        </p>
      </section>
    </Fragment>
  </CaseStudy>
</Base>

<script>
  // Read more: extend the essay in place, band stays pinned. Live, like the source.
  const more = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('.band__more');
  const extra = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.band__extra');
  more?.addEventListener('click', () => {
    const open = extra?.toggleAttribute('data-open') ?? false;
    more.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(open));
    more.textContent = open ? 'Read less' : 'Read more';
  });
</script>

<style>
  /* The rebuilt room, inverted: the full-bleed still becomes an ink field,
     and every owned word sits in one top band. Proportions transcribed from
     the reference: band baseline ~4% down, gutters ~2%, columns 3/3/6. */
  .site {
    position: relative;
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 10;
    background-color: var(--ink);
    color: var(--paper);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  /* Tonal echo of the portrait: a lighter mass low-centre, under a faint
     scan texture — the artwork's weight without the artwork. */
  .site::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background:
      repeating-linear-gradient(
        0deg,
        color-mix(in oklab, var(--paper) 4%, transparent) 0 1px,
        transparent 1px 4px
      ),
      radial-gradient(
        58% 72% at 54% 64%,
        color-mix(in oklab, var(--paper) 18%, transparent),
        transparent 72%
      );
  }

  .site__band {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 3.8% 2% auto;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(12, 1fr);
    column-gap: 1.5%;
    font-size: clamp(0.68rem, 1.35vw, 0.95rem);
    line-height: 1.45;
    z-index: 1;
  }
  .band__id {
    grid-column: 1 / 4;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }
  .band__links u {
    text-underline-offset: 0.18em;
  }

  .band__caption {
    grid-column: 4 / 7;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }
  /* The pairing the source trades on: italic serif display over a
     semi-mono roman credit, at the shared band size. */
  .band__title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-style: italic;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
  }
  .band__credit {
    font-size: 0.92em;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
  }

  .band__essay {
    grid-column: 7 / 13;
  }
  .band__essay p {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .band__extra {
    display: none;
  }
  .band__extra[data-open] {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 1em;
  }
  /* Read more sits one blank line under the essay, underlined like a link. */
  .band__more {
    margin-top: 1em;
    padding: 0;
    background: none;
    border: none;
    font: inherit;
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.18em;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .band__more:focus-visible {
    outline: var(--border-w, 2px) solid var(--spot, var(--paper));
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }

  /* Specimen credit for the echoed plate — mono, bottom margin, quiet. */
  .site__plate {
    position: absolute;
    left: 2%;
    bottom: 4%;
    font-size: var(--type-meta, 0.65rem);
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--paper) 55%, transparent);
    z-index: 1;
  }
</style>
